      "name": "rkcr",
      "username": "rkcr",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/b5ac83/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-11T23:53:08.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Due to an unlucky set of circumstances (namely, Bloodsworn Judgement), Chaos Lord ended up being placed underneath Kaargra Warfang. Chaos Lord makes it so that the first time you take damage each turn, you get to play the bottom card of your deck.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It completely broke the game to have it on Kaargra Warfang. Every time we hurt Kaargra Warfang she got to play another villain card. It was a three player game and each of us hit her + the environment, which meant the villain played 5 cards in one round. We lost quite quickly.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My question is - should we have not allowed that title to be played on her? Chaos Lord doesn't even look like it would normally be earnable by villains (it specifically mentions players + hero cards). But in this one case, she *can* earn it, but then it means game over (unless she happens to be at a low HP, but she was at ~35 HP when she earned the title).</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:18.554Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
