    {
      "id": 126871,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-12T03:21:43.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Chaos Lord is devastating to have on Kaargra. &nbsp;The only ways to clear it are flipping her, End of Days, or Adept's destruction that costs an instrument.</p><p>How I normally deal with Kaargra is get her down low in health, usually 5-10 based on environment damage and leave her until we can finish her off and reach 20 in the same round. &nbsp;There are times you have to go away from this, but you don't want to get rid of her and then have Bloodsworn Judgement hit right before you would win.</p><p>When she gains a title like Chaos Lord or The Seeker it changes the game drastically. &nbsp;Or the one game when she picked up Mindbreaker, and then was hit by the environment and gained the Indiscriminate, which with Captain Cosmic in the game soon led to Champion. &nbsp;That was a rough game, and we did not win.</p><p>We have 2 house rules we use with Kaargra Warfang:</p><p><span>1. &nbsp;The only title that does nothing under Kaargra Warfang is Living Weapon. &nbsp;We house-rule it to increase the first damage dealt by her each turn by 2.</span></p><div>2. &nbsp;We put titles back in the title deck once (H) are in the title area. &nbsp;We line them up in order they entered play, and when a new one comes into play (or returns from a destroyed target) if more than (H) are in play we put the oldest one back in the deck until only (H) are in play. &nbsp;Makes it easier to manage and makes Bloodsworn Judgement more threatening later in the game.</div>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:23.888Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
