      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Chaos Lord is devastating to have on Kaargra. &nbsp;The only ways to clear it are flipping her, End of Days, or Adept&#39;s destruction that costs an instrument.</p><p>How I normally deal with Kaargra is get her down low in health, usually 5-10 based on environment damage and leave her until we can finish her off and reach 20 in the same round. &nbsp;There are times you have to go away from this, but you don&#39;t want to get rid of her and then have Bloodsworn Judgement hit right before you would win.</p><p>When she gains a title like Chaos Lord or The Seeker it changes the game drastically. &nbsp;Or the one game when she picked up Mindbreaker, and then was hit by the environment and gained the Indiscriminate, which with Captain Cosmic in the game soon led to Champion. &nbsp;That was a rough game, and we did not win.</p><p>We have 2 house rules we use with Kaargra Warfang:</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">1. &nbsp;The only title that does nothing under Kaargra Warfang is Living Weapon. &nbsp;We house-rule it to increase the first damage dealt by her each turn by 2.</span></p><div>2. &nbsp;We put titles back in the title deck once (H) are in the title area. &nbsp;We line them up in order they entered play, and when a new one comes into play (or returns from a destroyed target) if more than (H) are in play we put the oldest one back in the deck until only (H) are in play. &nbsp;Makes it easier to manage and makes Bloodsworn Judgement more threatening later in the game.</div>",
