      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/ce7236/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-15T04:25:30.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Chaos Lord is devastating to have on Kaargra. &nbsp;The only ways to clear it are flipping her, End of Days, or Adept's destruction that costs an instrument.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>None of those would actually work. &nbsp;All of the title cards are not considered to be hero, villain, ongoing, equipment, or environment cards and plus they are indestructible so they can't be destroyed by any of those effects. &nbsp;And if they are on Kaargra then they can't be removed at all as long as she is a target, so you need to have her flip so she is no longer a target then destroy another target to move it back to the title area.</p>",
